IMAANAA CALL - VOICE/VIDEO CALL UPDATE

FILES
- server.js: replaces the project's root server.js
- package.json: replaces the project's root package.json
- public/app.js: replaces the existing public/app.js

IMPORTANT
Keep your existing public/index.html and other existing project files. Do not delete them.
Your public/index.html must load Socket.IO and SimplePeer before public/app.js, for example:
  <script src="/socket.io/socket.io.js"></script>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/simple-peer@9.11.1/simplepeer.min.js"></script>
  <script src="/app.js"></script>

RENDER
1. Upload/commit these files to the same GitHub repository.
2. In Render, keep Build Command: npm install
3. Keep Start Command: npm start
4. Set DATABASE_URL to your existing Neon PostgreSQL connection string.
5. Deploy and test with two accounts on two different phones/networks.

CELLULAR DATA / WEBRTC
The call uses the phone's browser microphone/camera and internet connection (mobile data or Wi-Fi). Camera/microphone access generally requires HTTPS, which Render provides on its public service URL.
STUN is included by default. Some mobile carriers/NATs require a TURN server for reliable audio/video. If using a TURN provider, set these Render environment variables:
- TURN_URLS = comma-separated TURN URLs, e.g. turn:your-turn-host:3478,turns:your-turn-host:5349
- TURN_USERNAME = the TURN username
- TURN_CREDENTIAL = the TURN credential/password
Use credentials from your TURN provider; do not put private TURN credentials into public source code.

This update does not itself provide free mobile data or bypass a customer's cellular data charges. Each phone needs internet access and an active data plan or Wi-Fi.

